# Beads Issue Tracking

This project uses [Beads (bd)](https://github.com/steveyegge/beads) for ALL task tracking.

## Core Rules

- Track ALL work in bd (never use markdown TODOs)
- Always commit `.beads/issues.jsonl` with code changes
- Git hooks auto-sync on commit/merge
- PR-backed Beads stay `open` or `in_progress` until their linked PR is merged
- Close PR-backed Beads only with `scripts/close-bead-after-merge.sh`

## Essential Commands

```bash
bd ready                              # Find unblocked work
bd create --title="..." --type=task --priority=2  # Create issue
bd update <id> --status=in_progress   # Claim work
bash scripts/close-bead-after-merge.sh <bead-id> <pr-number>  # After mergedAt
bd dep add <issue> <depends-on>       # Add dependency (issue depends on depends-on)
bd sync                               # Sync with git remote
```

**Issue types:** `bug`, `feature`, `task`, `epic`, `chore`
**Priorities:** `0` (critical) → `4` (backlog)

## Workflow

1. Find work: `bd ready`
2. Claim: `bd update <id> --status=in_progress`
3. Implement: Edit code, run `task test` and `task lint`
4. Merge the associated PR and verify its live `mergedAt`
5. Complete: `bash scripts/close-bead-after-merge.sh <bead-id> <pr-number>` and commit with `.beads/issues.jsonl`

